  "body": "## Change\n\nSelect one stable closed straight-sided DXF chain for a vertical Wire Contour operation. The generator and verifier now use the same boundary in the setup coordinate system. The existing wire generator applies the physical offset once. Other unselected chains do not become cuts.\n\nThe geometry resolver preserves original line and arc segments and the source placement. The generic wire path refuses curved or open selections. It also refuses an absent or stale selection, unsafe threading, missing holding and an insufficient stock envelope. The normal model-based operation keeps its behavior.\n\nThe operation stamp uses the exact source geometry. It caches that signature on the immutable drawing. Save, reopen and undo retain the selection. This is the straight closed-chain part of #2022. The separate inspection exporter for curved chains is under #3179.\n\n## Verification\n\nContributor head: `2d0fa64841a1b42dbacb330f75f6bab61897da10`. Base: `5e76e6a14b366c510858bbbf660c06ca013c34d4`.\n\nThe targeted author check passed 34 tests, including `placed_chain_posts_one_offset_and_retains_its_identity_on_reopen`, the three selected-chain regressions, the exact-source-signature pin and 30 existing wire tests. Strict all-target Clippy passed for the app and geometry crates.\n\nA synthetic project selected one of two disjoint contours. Its normal generic ISO post retained only the chosen offset loop. Reopening preserved its identity. The generic path still refuses circular segments. No physical cut or native-control test forms part of this generic post change.\n\nThe official heavy selector reached 236 release steps for motion and app. The full run is queued behind an active release target. It has no pass result yet. The targeted author check above is complete. Keep this PR in draft until the reached checks and the normal readiness pass are complete.\n\nEffort: high. No escalation.\n\nChangelog: Wire Contour can use one selected straight-sided DXF chain on stock with the normal wire verification.\n\nRefs #2022\n\nFixes #3180\n",
